
config HAS_CPUFREQ
	bool

config INTEL_HWP
	bool "Intel Hardware P-States driver" if EXPERT
	depends on INTEL && HAS_CPUFREQ
	default y
	help
	  The cpufreq=hwp driver, which lets Intel CPUs pick their own
	  performance state within limits Xen sets.  Without it, cpufreq=hwp
	  is an invalid option and leaves Xen without a cpufreq driver, as
	  any invalid cpufreq= value does.  The default ACPI P-state driver
	  is unaffected.

	  If unsure, say Y.

config AMD_CPPC
	bool "AMD CPPC driver" if EXPERT
	depends on AMD && HAS_CPUFREQ
	default y
	help
	  The cpufreq=amd-cppc driver, which drives AMD CPUs through ACPI
	  CPPC with the _CPC data the hardware domain uploads.  Without it,
	  cpufreq=amd-cppc is an invalid option and leaves Xen without a
	  cpufreq driver, as any invalid cpufreq= value does, and uploaded
	  CPPC data is ignored.  The default PowerNow! driver is unaffected.

	  If unsure, say Y.

config CPUFREQ_GOV_ONDEMAND
	bool "Ondemand cpufreq governor" if EXPERT
	depends on HAS_CPUFREQ
	default y
	help
	  The ondemand governor, which scales each CPU's frequency with its
	  load, and which is Xen's default governor.  Without it, the default
	  governor is performance, and asking for ondemand, with
	  cpufreq=xen:ondemand or at run time through XEN_SYSCTL_pm_op, fails.

	  If unsure, say Y.
